            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="0589" n="577" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg577"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890F.6363/26: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-05T13:00:00+03:06">June 5, 1942—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 7—11:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Referring to cable May 19<anchor n="35" xml:id="d689-f1"/> and despatch May
                    22 from Cairo.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d689-f2"/> Should Department discuss with
                    Ohliger problem of defense and denial operations at Dhahran, sight should not be
                    lost of desirability of utilizing American military forces if needed and
                    practicable and of protecting insofar as possible oil concession rights and oil
                    company personnel by inducting active American participants into United States
                    Army and by giving timely notice to Saudi Government through this Legation of
                    Army’s intentions.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
